        {
          "name": "Act on contact message",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{accessToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}",
                "description": "HMAC admin session from POST /admin/session. Missing/invalid token → 401 before host or id checks."
              },
              {
                "key": "x-school-host",
                "value": "{{adminHost}}",
                "description": "Must be admin.<rootHost> after port strip. Checked only after a valid admin token."
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/contact-messages/{{contactMessageId}}/act",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "admin",
                "contact-messages",
                "{{contactMessageId}}",
                "act"
              ],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "contactMessageId",
                  "value": "{{contactMessageId}}",
                  "description": "UUID from GET /admin/contact-messages (first row). Public POST /public/contact does not return this id. Invalid or unknown UUID → 404 Message not found."
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Marks a contact message acted (`actedAt` set). **No JSON body.** Empty body is fine — the handler does not call `readJsonBody`.\n\n**Auth:** required. Same `requireAdminSession` gate as the list: **401 first**, then host, then method, then id. Missing/invalid/school HMAC → `401 { \"error\": \"Unauthorized\" }` even on a school host.\n\n**Who:** the signed-in platform operator.\n\n**Host (required after auth):** `rejectIfNotAdminHost`. Wrong host → `403 { \"error\": \"This action is only allowed on the admin host\" }`.\n\n**Path:** `readAdminContactMessageAct` matches `/admin/contact-messages/:id/act` where `:id` is non-empty and contains no `/`. `/admin/contact-messages/act` and nested paths do **not** match this handler (generic `404 { \"error\": \"Not found\" }`).\n\n**Id:** `isContactMessageId` — UUID regex (any version/variant, case-insensitive). Non-UUID (`not-a-uuid`) **and** unknown UUID both → `404 { \"error\": \"Message not found\" }`. There is no 400 for a bad id.\n\n**Idempotent:** acting twice still **200** `{ message }` with `acted: true` (store returns the existing row).\n\n**Side effects:** sets `actedAt` once. Does not delete the row. Later lists keep the row but sort unacted first; `pending` decreases by one on the first act.\n\n**Success `200`:** `{ \"message\": { id, school, name, role, email, note, phone, created, acted: true } }` — same view as the list.\n\n**Errors that exist:** 401 Unauthorized; 403 admin-host only; 404 Message not found; 405 if not POST (GET/PUT/PATCH/DELETE). 405 only after a valid admin token.\n\n**Not used:** 400, 409, 422. No distinct 500 from this handler."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  pm.test('acted message is { message } with acted true', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('message').that.is.an('object');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.message.id).to.be.a('string');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.message.school).to.be.a('string');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.message.name).to.be.a('string');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.message.email).to.be.a('string');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.message.note).to.be.a('string');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.message.created).to.be.a('string');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.message.acted).to.eql(true);",
                  "    pm.expect(body.message).to.have.property('role');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.message).to.have.property('phone');",
                  "  });",
                  "}",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 401) {",
                  "  pm.test('unauthenticated is 401 with Unauthorized', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.error).to.eql('Unauthorized');",
                  "  });",
                  "}",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 403) {",
                  "  pm.test('admin host required', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.error).to.eql('This action is only allowed on the admin host');",
                  "  });",
                  "}",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 404) {",
                  "  pm.test('unknown or invalid id', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.error).to.eql('Message not found');",
                  "  });",
                  "}",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 405) {",
                  "  pm.test('method not allowed', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.error).to.eql('Method not allowed');",
                  "  });",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
